note S3 layout: every integer field type, both byte orders, scalar and array fields, run-time and constant
note indexes, an inline function with a layout parameter, the raw uchar fallback and len. Writes the 40-byte
note image to stdout, then exits 0 when every read-back matches (else the failing check's number).
om2
layout mix 40
field sb byte at 0 little
field ss short at 1 big
field si int at 3 little
field sl long at 7 big
field us ushort 2 at 15 big
field ui uint 2 at 19 little
field ul ulong at 27 little
field tail uchar 5 at 35 big
end
fn setul c edit mix v ulong to void inline
put c ul v
end
fn fill c edit mix k ulong to void
put c sb -2
put c ss -300
put c si -70000
put c sl -4294967296
put c us 0 0xbeef
put c us k 0x1234
put c ui 0 0xdeadbeef
put c ui k 7
setul c 0x0102030405060708
for i ulong 5
put c tail i uchar add i 0xa0
end
end
fn check c view mix k ulong to int
if ne get c sb -2
ret 1
end
if ne get c ss -300
ret 2
end
if ne get c si -70000
ret 3
end
if ne get c sl -4294967296
ret 4
end
if ne get c us 0 0xbeef
ret 5
end
if ne get c us k 0x1234
ret 6
end
if ne get c ui 0 0xdeadbeef
ret 7
end
if ne get c ui k 7
ret 8
end
if ne get c ul 0x0102030405060708
ret 9
end
if ne get c tail 4 0xa4
ret 10
end
if ne get c 1 254
ret 11
end
if ne len c 40
ret 12
end
ret 0
end
fn main to int
c = new uchar 40 0
fill c 1
w = write 1 c 0 40
ret check c 1
end
